physocarpus opulifolius or  nine bark is a native shrub that's been  highly hybridized to produce  different color leaves this you see  purple sometimes yellow  sometimes green but the distinctive  feature  is the lobing of the leaves the two  lobes toward the base of the leaf  and then a longer lobe in the middle  this is visocarpus opulofolius nine bark
 

